  "requires": [
    "chain/1"
  ],
  "dispatch": [
    {
      "address": "register",
      "sender": "$owner",
      "program": "overlay"
    },
    {
      "address": "",
      "sender": "event",
      "program": "overlay"
    },
    {
      "address": "",
      "sender": "$self",
      "program": "overlay"
    },
    {
      "address": "",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-p2p"
    },
    {
      "address": "amm-p2p",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-p2p"
    },
    {
      "address": "submit",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "overlay",
      "filter": "beef"
    },
    {
      "transport": "http",
      "address": "/call",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-p2p",
      "fn": "call"
    },
    {
      "transport": "libp2p",
      "address": "/amm-validator/1/swap",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-validator",
      "fn": "swap"
    },
    {
      "transport": "libp2p",
      "address": "/amm-validator/1/addLiquidity",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-validator",
      "fn": "addLiquidity"
    },
    {
      "transport": "libp2p",
      "address": "/amm-validator/1/deploy",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-validator",
      "fn": "deploy"
    }
  ],
  "reads": [
    {
      "address": "/listTopicManagers",
      "program": "overlay",
      "fn": "listTopicManagers"
    },
    {
      "address": "/listLookupServiceProviders",
      "program": "overlay",
      "fn": "listLookupServiceProviders"
    },
    {
      "address": "/getDocumentationForTopicManager",
      "program": "overlay",
      "fn": "topicDocumentation"
    },
    {
      "address": "/getDocumentationForLookupServiceProvider",
      "program": "overlay",
      "fn": "lookupDocumentation"
    },
    {
      "address": "/mandala/tokens",
      "program": "mandala-lookup",
      "fn": "tokens"
    },
    {
      "address": "/",
      "prefix": true,
      "program": "amm-p2p",
      "fn": "serve",
      "root": "www",
      "index": "index.html"
    }
  ],
  "description": "An AMM over Mandala tokens (docs/AMM.md): the overlay engine (shruggr/skein-overlay 0.9.2, required: chain/1) with the Mandala components (shruggr/skein-mandala 0.7.5: the topic manager mandala-topic, one topic per token tm_<txid> and the discovery topic tm_mandala; the lookups ls_mandala and ls_mandala_deploys; the token list, the read /mandala/tokens of mandala-lookup), the pool liquidity lookup ls_amm (amm-lookup, one service over every token topic, each query naming its token), the validator (amm-validator: swap, addLiquidity, deploy as libp2p direct calls; it submits the signed transaction to its own overlay by message, {fn: \"submit\"} in the box submit (<app>/submit), and answers the call on the engine's answer) and amm-p2p: the marketplace relay (amm.swap/1, amm.pool/1, amm.liquidity/1: a taker's or an LP's transaction carried to the validator the caller names by identity key and libp2p peer ID, dialled, or handed in-VM to this instance's own amm-validator when that peer is this node) and the pages, www/ served from the app's own tree (skein-sdk files.serve) by the read / (a call: anyone, signed or not, nothing logged; shruggr/skein#135), beside the engine's listing and documentation reads and its derived /lookup; the http rows (/call, the derived /submit) are message routes: a signed request. Anyone submits to the engine by message in the box submit (<app>/submit), answered by message, or by POST /submit, BRC-22: it waits and answers the STEAK (skein-overlay 0.9.1+); the app's own box <app> is amm-p2p's. The manifest declares no topics: the owner registers each token topic with the engine, a message in the app's box register (<app>/register once installed) {fn: \"register\", args: {topic, program: \"mandala-topic\"}}, and drops it with {fn: \"deregister\", args: {topic}}. Market and validator are two roles of the engine (shruggr/skein#120, 0.6.0), the owner's switch (0.6.2, skein-overlay 0.9.2): {fn: \"market\", args: {window} | {off: true}} / {fn: \"validator\", args: {every} | {off: true}} in <app>/register (the Market and Validator switches on the mandala/tokens/ page), kept beside the registered set in <app>/topics, over config.overlay.market / .validator (the initial value, e.g. --config at install): with the market on {window: ms} a register also asks the runtime's liveness tool for the topic's tm_<txid>-live beats (liveness, window), served at GET /amm/.live/tm_<txid>-live, which the pages read to name a validator; with the validator on {every: ms} it also beacons tm_<txid>-live every that many ms (beacon, no body: the frame carries the instance's identity key, the gossip message its peer ID), and amm-validator signs swaps and takes on new liquidity (addLiquidity, deploy) for any registered token, refusing them not_validating without it. A deregister reverses both; switching a role emits for every registered token. This manifest sets neither: both are off until the owner turns one on."
}
